BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Diwali / Deepavali / दीपावली
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:diwali-2026-11-09@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals
DESCRIPTION:Why: light the home when the moon is dark — invite prosperity
 \, kinship and clarity after the ancestral fortnight.\n\nStory: Diwali (De
 epavali) on the amavasya of Ashvina (amanta) / Kartika lights lamps for Ra
 ma's return and Lakshmi's grace in the darkest new-moon night.\nSource: Ra
 mayana return narrative\; Padma Purana Lakshmi strands\nWhy: light the hom
 e when the moon is dark — invite prosperity\, kinship and clarity after 
 the ancestral fortnight.\nModern angle: Light\, gathering and gift rituals
  support mood and social ties in dark season\; cultural/psychological with
  seasonal-affect context.\nEvidence: Cultural/psychological\nMore: https:/
 /saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/reasoning.html#calendar-lunisol
 ar\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timing coming later.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/calendar.html#11c9bda
