BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Makar Sankranti / मकर संक्रांति
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:makar_sankranti-2027-01-15@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals\,sankranti\,birth-auspicious
DESCRIPTION:Why: solar astronomy made visible as a festival of harvest\, ch
 arity (daan)\, and sesame–jaggery offerings to Surya.\n\nStory: Makar Sa
 nkranti marks the Sun's sidereal ingress into Makara (Capricorn)\, traditi
 onally linked with Uttarayana — the northward turn of the solar path.\nS
 ource: Surya Siddhanta\; Puranic Uttarayana lore\nWhy: solar astronomy mad
 e visible as a festival of harvest\, charity (daan)\, and sesame–jaggery
  offerings to Surya.\nModern angle: Corresponds to a real solar-longitude 
 event (sidereal Capricorn ingress). Seasonal marker near mid-winter in the
  northern hemisphere.\nEvidence: Established\nLink: https://www.drikpancha
 ng.com/sankranti/makar-sankranti-date-time.html\nMore: https://saumya-shar
 ma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/reasoning.html#sankranti-solar-ingress\nLoc
 ation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timing coming later.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/calendar.html#350fff9
 e725b595c
END:VEVENT
