BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maha Shivaratri / महा शिवरात्रि
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270306
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270307
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:maha_shivaratri-2027-03-07@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals
DESCRIPTION:Why: a night vigil of remembrance and restraint at the dark for
 tnight's edge\, traditionally linked to Shiva's cosmic dance and marriage 
 lore.\n\nStory: Maha Shivaratri is the great night of Shiva\, observed on 
 the Krishna Chaturdashi before Magha/Phalguna amavasya — vigil\, fasting
  and bilva offerings.\nSource: Shiva Purana\; Linga Purana\nWhy: a night v
 igil of remembrance and restraint at the dark fortnight's edge\, tradition
 ally linked to Shiva's cosmic dance and marriage lore.\nModern angle: Nigh
 t-vigil fasting overlaps with researched intermittent-fasting windows\; ev
 idence for specific Shivaratri outcomes is cultural\, not clinical.\nEvide
 nce: Cultural/psychological\nLink: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/4070134
 7/\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/reasoning.html
 #ekadashi-fasting\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timing coming 
 later.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/calendar.html#d4bc313
