BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holika Dahan / होलिका दहन
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270321
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270322
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:holi-2027-03-22@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals
DESCRIPTION:Why: burn the symbol of harm\, then meet neighbours with colour
  — a ritual of courage\, play and community repair at winter's end.\n\nS
 tory: Holika Dahan on Phalguna Purnima recalls Prahlada's faith and Holika
 's fall\; the next day\, Rangwali Holi celebrates colour\, spring and soci
 al renewal.\nSource: Bhagavata Purana (Prahlada–Hiranyakashipu)\nWhy: bu
 rn the symbol of harm\, then meet neighbours with colour — a ritual of c
 ourage\, play and community repair at winter's end.\nModern angle: Strong 
 social-bonding and seasonal festival effects\; no medical claim for the fi
 re ritual itself.\nEvidence: Cultural/psychological\nMore: https://saumya-
 sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/reasoning.html#calendar-lunisolar\nLoca
 tion basis: New Delhi. City-specific timing coming later.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
