  vulnerable at the spring new-year fortnight.\n\nStory: Ram Navami celebra
 tes the birth of Rama on Chaitra Shukla Navami — Maryada Purushottam\, t
 he ideal of dharmic kingship in the Ramayana.\nSource: Valmiki Ramayana\; 
 later Puranic calendars\nWhy: remember a life-model of duty\, restraint an
 d care for the vulnerable at the spring new-year fortnight.\nModern angle:
  Narrative ethics and community worship\; cultural meaning\, not a scienti
 fic outcome claim.\nEvidence: Cultural/psychological\nMore: https://saumya
 -sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/reasoning.html#calendar-lunisolar\nLoc
 ation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timing coming later.
