DESCRIPTION:Why: pause at the full moon of Ashadha to name gratitude for th
 ose who taught you how to see.\n\nStory: Guru Purnima (Ashadha Purnima) ho
 nours the teacher — traditionally Vyasa\, and by extension every guide w
 ho transmits knowledge.\nSource: Skanda Purana / Vyasa Puja tradition\nWhy
 : pause at the full moon of Ashadha to name gratitude for those who taught
  you how to see.\nModern angle: Gratitude practices show measurable well-b
 eing links in psychology research\; the lunar date is cultural.\nEvidence:
  Plausible\nLink: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12585811/\nMore: https:/
 /saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/reasoning.html#calendar-lunisol
