DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:janmashtami-2027-09-23@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals
DESCRIPTION:Why: stay awake into the night to welcome a story of divine car
 e arriving in fragile human form.\n\nStory: Janmashtami marks Krishna's bi
 rth at midnight on Krishna Ashtami of Bhadrapada (amanta) — the Gokula n
 arrative of protection amid danger.\nSource: Bhagavata Purana Canto 10\nWh
 y: stay awake into the night to welcome a story of divine care arriving in
  fragile human form.\nModern angle: Night vigil and fasting are cultural-d
 evotional\; community singing supports belonging.\nEvidence: Cultural/psyc
 hological\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/reasoni
 ng.html#calendar-lunisolar\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timin
 g coming later.
